# Always install devDependencies, even when NODE_ENV=production.
#
# This exists because of a real deploy failure, not as a preference. Render (and Heroku, and
# most CI images) set NODE_ENV=production on the service, which npm reads: when NODE_ENV is
# production, npm defaults `omit` to `dev` and skips devDependencies entirely.
#
# This repo *builds* on the server — `tsc` compiles apps/api, and TypeScript itself plus every
# `@types/*` package are devDependencies. So `npm ci` succeeded, then the build died with a
# wall of errors that pointed nowhere near the real cause:
#
#   src/routes/paypal.ts(1,24): error TS7016: Could not find a declaration file for module
#   'express'. Try `npm i --save-dev @types/express` if it exists...
#
# @types/express *was* installed in package.json — it just hadn't been installed on the box.
# The suggested fix ("npm i --save-dev @types/express") would have changed nothing.
#
# Verified: `NODE_ENV=production npm config get omit` prints `dev` without this file, and
# nothing with it.
#
# Setting it here rather than in the build command means it applies to every environment that
# builds this repo, including ones nobody has configured yet.
include=dev
